SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] OJJDP FY 2026 Opioid Affected Youth Initiative — due
DESCRIPTION:Grants of up to $750K over 36 months for states\, local governments\, tribes and nonprofits to run prevention\, intervention and treatment for children\, youth and families affected by opioid\, stimulant and other SUDs\, in partnership with justice and child-welfare agencies. MORE fits as clinician training (subrecipient or consultant line) inside the parent/family treatment and recovery part of an application (Objective 3). The youth-only prevention parts are a weaker fit\, and MORE's evidence base is in adults.\n\nPath: Sub · Priority 2.0\nhttps://www.ojp.gov/funding/docs/ojjdp-2026-172748.pdf
URL:https://www.ojp.gov/funding/docs/ojjdp-2026-172748.pdf
